    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d397">

                <pb facs="0349" n="339" sameAs="frus:frus1949v08/pg339"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/5–2149: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Taipei</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Edgar</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Taipei</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-05-21T16:00:00+09:00">May 21, 1949—4 p.
                            m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received May 22—6:41 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>181. Persistent rumor in Taiwan that top level Kmt conference in preparation
                    there. Local officials vacating residences for exalted guests. K. C. Wu<anchor
                        n="33" xml:id="d397-f1"/> and Tao Hsi-sheng<anchor n="34" xml:id="d397-f2"/>
                    there now. Generalissimo expected. Constant rumors Generalissimo already in
                    Taiwan but best information says still Yangtze anchorage although quarters at
                    Sun-Moon Lake and Taipei have been prepared.</p>
                <p>Sent Department 181, repeated Canton 42, Shanghai 145.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Edgar</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d397-f1" n="33" xml:id="d397-f1-content">
                <p>Former Mayor of Shanghai.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d397-f2" n="34" xml:id="d397-f2-content">
                <p>Chinese Vice Minister of the Kuomintang Ministry of Information.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
